  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 510.14 Registration Refund for Members of Armed Forces",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 510.14 Registration Refund for Members of Armed Forces.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 261:68, any person who is ordered into or enlists in the military or naval services during a war emergency may request an abeyance of their registration(s) during such service.\n\n(b) An application may be made in writing and submitted, in person to any substation or by mail, to:\n\nThe Division of Motor Vehicles, Registration Bureau\n\n23 Hazen Drive\n\nConcord, N.H. 03305.\n\n(c) Each applicant shall submit the following:\n\n(1) The name, legal address, and date of birth of the member of the armed services;\n\n(2) A copy of military orders; and\n\n(3) The plate number of the vehicle to be considered for refund.\n\n(d) Upon receipt of the information set forth in (c) above, the department shall grant a pro rata refund, based upon the number of months the vehicle is unused.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500) ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12 (from Saf-C 511.15); ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 510.13)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
}
